  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Consider the inequality\n$$\\left|x+\\frac{1}{x}\\right|<2x$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Explain why $x$ must be positive.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2x>\\left|x+\\frac1x\\right|\\ge0$, so $x>0$.",
          "worked": "Since $\\left|x+\\frac1x\\right|\\ge0$ and $\\left|x+\\frac1x\\right|<2x$, we have $2x>0$. Hence $x>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence explain why $x+\\frac{1}{x}$ must be positive.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "A positive number plus its reciprocal is positive.",
          "worked": "Since $x>0$, its reciprocal $\\frac1x>0$. Therefore $x+\\frac1x>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Solve the inequality.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x>1$.",
          "worked": "From parts a and b, $x>0$ and $x+\\frac1x>0$, so the absolute value can be removed. Multiplying by $x^2>0$ gives\n$$\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac1x&<2x\\\\x^3+x&<2x^3\\\\-x^3+x&<0\\\\x^3-x&>0\\\\x(x^2-1)&>0\\\\x(x-1)(x+1)&>0.\\end{aligned}$$\nThe product is positive for $-1<x<0$ or $x>1$. Since $x>0$, the solution is $x>1$. Since $x+\\frac1x>0$, no negative-argument case is needed.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      }
    ]
  },
